      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ba8bd60a-e86a-5439-823a-fbaac32bf4b1",
        ":question/problem": "Find the exact value of the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ whose tangent has a slope of $1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+4x-3) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =2(2x)+4(1) \\\\  & =4x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4 & =1 \\\\ 4x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $1$ at the point where $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
