      "question": {
        ":question/id": "ac72967c-0395-50e5-812a-2bfe9c19348f",
        ":question/problem": "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points on the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+20\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+6\\cdot 2x+20\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}+12x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{\u2032}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+12x+20 & =2 \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6({x}^{2}-2x-3) & =0 \\\\ -6(x+1)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the points where $x=-1,3.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
